BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//notapattern//calendar export 1.0//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
METHOD:PUBLISH
X-WR-CALNAME:The Amish Project
X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Amish Project
DTSTART:20270211T010000Z
DTEND:20270211T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20261118T003407Z
UID:1012758
DESCRIPTION:<p>When tragedy shatters a close-knit Amish community\, what f
 ollows is an extraordinary act of grace that challenges everything we thin
 k we know about forgiveness.<br /><br />This spring\, Tony Award&reg\; win
 ner Jonathan Groff returns to Broadway in a tour de force performance in <
 em>The Amish Project</em>\, a deeply moving solo play about the astonishin
 g power of compassion in the face of unimaginable loss.<br /><br />Inspire
 d by true events that unfolded just minutes from where Groff grew up\, <em
 >The Amish Project</em> is an intimate portrait of a place and a community
  channeled through a single performer. Written by acclaimed playwright Jes
 sica Dickey and directed by Sarna Lapine (<em>Sunday in the Park with Geor
 ge</em>)\, this remarkable story invites us to reflect on how\, even in th
 e darkest of hours\, our shared humanity endures.</p>
LOCATION:Broadhurst Theatre\, 235 West 44th Street\, New York NY 10036
URL:https://www.telecharge.com/The-Amish-Project-Tickets
END:VEVENT
